course: dictionary
lesson: 14029
title: Malpractice: bad work by professionals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Malpractice is a long word, but you can work out its meaning from the clues around it. It starts with mal-, which means bad, as in malfunction. Practice here means the work someone does in their job.
explain: «The surgeon made a careless mistake, and the patient was badly hurt.» When a doctor, lawyer or other professional does their job very badly or carelessly and someone is harmed, that is malpractice. When the job is medicine, we call it medical malpractice.
explain: The word also means dishonest behaviour in a job. «Mia hid notes under her desk and copied answers during the test.» In UK schools this is called exam malpractice, and it can cancel your results. To check your meaning, swap in a simpler word like wrongdoing and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Malpractice means bad or careless work by a professional, or wrong and dishonest behaviour in a job.
fact: «Medical malpractice» means a doctor's serious mistake that harms a patient.
fact: «Exam malpractice» means cheating in exams, such as copying or having a phone in the exam room.
fact: Exam malpractice can cancel your results.
fact: A patient harmed by medical malpractice may take the doctor to court.
exercise: «The surgeon's careless mistake hurt her patient.» What is this an example of? | A lucky escape | Good teaching | Exam practice | *Medical malpractice
exercise: «Mia had notes hidden under her desk during the test.» What is this? | Good revision | Sports practice | A healthy snack | *Exam malpractice
exercise: Which word best matches "wrong or dishonest behaviour in a job"? | *Malpractice | Holiday | Generosity | Kindness
test: «The lawyer was sued for malpractice after losing his client's money.» What does sued for malpractice mean? | *The lawyer was taken to court for doing the job badly | The lawyer was asked to teach a class | The lawyer won a prize for hard work | The lawyer was given a medal
test: Which of these is an example of exam malpractice? | *Copying answers from a friend during a test | Reading a book in the library | Writing a neat summary | Walking to school in the rain
exam: What is the best meaning of malpractice? | A type of exam paper | A famous doctor | A kind and helpful way of working | *Wrong or careless work, or dishonest behaviour, by a professional
